            "src/main/java/ZigZag.java",
            "pure-rule; static int[][] traversal(int size, boolean[][] reserved) implements two-pass bounded serpentine traversal over unreserved cells only. First pass counts only unreserved cells with int count = 0, then literally allocates int[][] result = new int[count][2];. Second pass iterates rows 0..size-1; even rows visit columns 0..size-1 ascending, odd rows visit columns size-1..0 descending; appends [row,col] only when !reserved[row][col]. No while loops; MUST NOT allocate new int[size * size][2]; MUST NOT terminate on index < size * size; no placeholder entries."
        ],
        [
            "src/main/java/FinderPattern.java",
            "pure-rule; three-finder reserved mask definition and enforcement. static boolean[][] reservedMask(int size) marks three 7x7 finder squares at top-left, top-right, bottom-left; rejects size < 21 or even. static void place(QRMatrix) sets those finder cells true. static void verify(QRMatrix) enforces that those exact reserved cells are true and others remain unreserved; throws IllegalArgumentException on mismatch. Mask used consistently by traversal, place, and verify."
        ],
        [
