            "pure-rule; framing and bit conversions with exact padding and MSB-first rules. Methods: encodePayload(String text) builds frame [lenHi,lenLo,payload,checksum]; checksum computed ONLY over prefix via java.util.Arrays.copyOf(frame, frame.length - 1) and Checksum.sumMod256; never over complete frame. decodePayload(byte[] frame) requires exact length 2+L+1, validates checksum using the same prefix-only java.util.Arrays.copyOf(frame, frame.length - 1) and compares to (frame[frame.length - 1] & 0xFF); returns strict UTF-8 String. bytesToBits(byte[] bytes) emits exactly eight MSB-first bits per byte with the literal assignment bits[i * 8 + bit] = (bytes[i] & (1 << (7 - bit))) != 0;; bitsToBytes(boolean[] bits) accepts any length including non-multiples of eight, literally allocates byte[] result = new byte[(bits.length + 7) / 8]; and sets bits with result[i / 8] |= (byte) (1 << (7 - (i % 8)));; no modulo-length rejection or truncation."
        ],
